Expedited Preliminary Plat | UDC-20-00174
9

FINAL PLAT DATA:  In reviewing, providing comments, and making recommendations and decisions on
a proposed final plat, the Staff, Planning Commission and City Council shall use the following 3 criteria, as
found in Section 2.1.3.d:
1. The layout and design of the final plat is in substantial compliance with the approved preliminary
plat considering the number of lots or parcels, street and block layout, and access, and any
deviations in the final plat brings the application in further compliance with the Comprehensive
Plan.
2. The application meets any conditions or modifications of the approved preliminary plat.
3. The application meets the purposes, intent, and applicable standards of Article 4.
As this plat is being pursued as an expedited application, review criteria 1 and 2 are not applicable.
Review criterion 3 is also found in the Preliminary Plat process (as criterion 3) and is covered in
subsection 3 above.

REVIEW

The following agencies were asked to review the proposed project: 911/Combined Communications,
Black Hills Energy, Board of Public Utilities (BOPU), Building Department, CenturyLink, Charter,
Community Recreation and Events, Emergency Management, Engineering, Environmental Health
Department, Fire Department, Laramie County Assessor, Laramie County Attorney, Laramie County Clerk,
Laramie County School District #1, Metropolitan Planning Office, and Planning and Development.

COMMENTS FROM REVIEWING AGENCIES:
-
(Fulfilled by revised submittal) Please show the water service connection for 511 and 513 on
Lot 3 on the Preliminary Plat Map.
-
(FYI) Note that lots are not divisible until proper individual BOPU service lines are installed. Until
installation, Northland Holdings LLC will be required to enter into a common water and sewer
service connection agreement with the Board of Public Utilities for lots 2 and 3.
-
(FYI) Lots 1 and 2 are proposed to be SD3 lot types. With existing structures, these lots do not
meet minimum setbacks. Variance to these deficiencies (UDC-19-00618) approved November 21,
2019.
-
(FYI) Lot 3 is proposed to be a MD2 lot. With existing structures, this lot does not meet
minimum frontage or maximum setback. Variance to these deficiencies (UDC-19-00618)
approved November 21, 2019.
-
(Fulfilled by revised submittal)  Remove the original plat’s lots and the “Draft” watermark
from the Final Plat Map.
-
(Fulfilled by revised submittal) Suggest modification to Note 4 to have the last variance
listed as “e” or combine “b” and “c” (such that each variance is its own letter or each lot is its
own letter).
-
(FYI) Property appears to fulfill exemption requirements of UDC 4.2.5.c - no fees would be due
at time of plat signing.
-
(FYI) Plat largely appears to meet all review criteria and eligibility for an expedited plat.
-
(Fulfilled by revised submittal) Sidewalk will need to be added along Thomes.

OTHER COMMENTS RECEIVED:
-
None

